# items-teleport plan (this version, built on tune-v20-L1c / tune-fight-2s):
# 1. Keep the proven shard split (treasure, jungle health, strength or focus by role) and the altar lock.
# 2. Buy one teleport crystal from the gold left after shards (10 gold, once per champion).
# 3. Spend it on the altar walk: when a safe altar tile is within 3 tiles, teleport onto it, skipping the walk under fire.
# 4. Everything else (fights, camps, retreat, bag rules) is unchanged.
# mobility: escape dash at 50% health when an enemy champion is within 5 (dash home before the 30% recall line)
# Mobility plan (this version):
# 1. Teleport stays on the altar walk: a 3-turn channel is too slow to escape a fight, so it skips idle walking only.
# 2. Escape dashes: at half health with an enemy champion within 5, dash toward spawn early, while the dash can still save the champion.
# 3. Dash casts are fuel-gated (slot_is_dash and ability_ready checks inside dash_to) so 100x100 turns stay under the cap.
# 4. Recall timing is unchanged: safe recall only with no enemy within 8, so the 5-turn channel is not cancelled by a fight.
# gem-conversion plan (this version):
# 1. Bank a bag of 10+ gems at once when an enemy champion is within 8 (a carrier that dies drops everything to the killer).
# 2. Carriers far from an altar (altar_eta > 4) with enemies in sight step into an adjacent bush to break their line of sight.
# 3. Fights, camps, shards and the altar lock are unchanged, so the only new risk is the short bush step.
# 4. All new blocks sit behind fuel_remaining() gates and reuse the foes list (no extra enemy query).

# zg14: ability-type-aware casting from hybrid #14 (Opus): shield/heal on self, dash kept for escape/travel
def cast_on(slot, u):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_shield(slot) or slot_is_heal(slot):
            cast_self(slot)
        elif not slot_is_dash(slot):
            cast_at_unit(slot, u)

def dash_to(slot, t):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_dash(slot):
            dash_towards(slot, t)

