# tune-fight-2s [tune line]: tune-fight-2 (job G2: v19 + a ward on a bush within 2, 57.4% vs v19) with a cheaper ward: ward our own tile when standing in a bush (one bitboard test, no filter over bushes())
# tune-fight-2 [tune line]: league tune-fight2-g1 #19; beat tune-v19 57.4% head to head on 800 fresh games; cambc-exact vs tune-v19 0.537.
# line: tune
# vision-ward: tune-r-all-v2 + a ward on a bush within 2 tiles when walking a camp trip with no enemy visible.
# Bushes block enemy vision, so a ward placed in one hides the path of a camp walk. Fuel-gated, no new lets.
# coord-pack: before round 150 a champion with no ally in sight leaves elk/golem-sized camps alone and takes wolves; a champion walking to a big group (>= 60 threat) writes its threat level into shared byte 7 bits 2-7 as a call, and lone champions that read the call may join the elk camps.
# PLAN (team coordination, shared byte 7 bits 2-7 only):
# 1. Deaths come from 2+ enemies arriving together, so a lone champion must not start a 60+ threat camp early.
# 2. Big-group commitment is signalled by writing floor(threat/60) into bits 2-7 of byte 7 (bits 0-1 kept).
# 3. A lone champion (no ally visible within 6, no call in shared memory) walks to the nearest non-elk camp.
# 4. Once a call is up, lone champions may take elk camps too, so the team gathers on the same group.
# 5. Late game (round 150+) and any champion with an ally in sight behave as before.
