# items-teleport plan (this version, built on tune-v20-L1c / tune-fight-2s):
# 1. Keep the proven shard split (treasure, jungle health, strength or focus by role) and the altar lock.
# 2. Buy one teleport crystal from the gold left after shards (10 gold, once per champion).
# 3. Spend it on the altar walk: when a safe altar tile is within 3 tiles, teleport onto it, skipping the walk under fire.
# 4. Everything else (fights, camps, retreat, bag rules) is unchanged.
# pair-axis: outnumbered (2+ enemies visible and more enemies than allies within 4) -> raise the danger beacon (byte 7 bits 2-7), cast, step out, end turn; no committing dashes while the beacon is up.
# PLAN (pair axis): (a) never commit to a fight 2-vs-1: the outnumbered test is per turn, and the response is cast + step away, not a walk to allies (measured bad).
# (b) the beacon tells partners that a fight is going badly; while it is up, camp walks skip optional dashes and do not chase far goals.
# (c) the beacon clears when no enemy is visible, so stale fear never freezes farming.
# (d) fights stay one-on-one where we are the stronger side: the weakest in-range enemy is still the target.

# zg14: ability-type-aware casting from hybrid #14 (Opus): shield/heal on self, dash kept for escape/travel
def cast_on(slot, u):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_shield(slot) or slot_is_heal(slot):
            cast_self(slot)
        elif not slot_is_dash(slot):
            cast_at_unit(slot, u)

def dash_to(slot, t):
    if ability_ready(slot):
        if slot_is_dash(slot):
            dash_towards(slot, t)

